%% Recovery sequence: ReadControlFile -> StartupXLOG -> Startup* hooks -> WAL
%% replay -> Trim* -> consistent.

sequenceDiagram
    participant Postmaster
    participant Startup as Startup process
    participant CF as pg_control
    participant WAL
    participant SLRU as SLRU subsystems
    participant Standby as Standby readers

    Postmaster->>Startup: fork
    Startup->>CF: ReadControlFile()
    CF-->>Startup: ControlFileData<br/>{checkPointCopy.redo,<br/>nextXid, nextOid,<br/>nextMulti, oldestXid,...}

    Note over Startup: Validate magic, CRC,<br/>pg_control_version,<br/>catalog_version_no.

    Startup->>SLRU: BootStrap* / *ShmemInit
    Startup->>SLRU: StartupCLOG()<br/>(no-op: lazy reads)
    Startup->>SLRU: StartupCommitTs()
    Startup->>SLRU: StartupSUBTRANS(oldestActiveXID)<br/>(zero-fills the in-RAM page<br/>covering oldestActiveXID)
    Startup->>SLRU: StartupMultiXact()<br/>(MultiXactSetNextMXact;<br/>load from pg_control)

    Startup->>WAL: PerformWalRecovery()<br/>from checkPointCopy.redo

    loop for each WAL record
        WAL-->>Startup: record
        Startup->>SLRU: rmgr-specific redo<br/>(clog_redo, multixact_redo,<br/>commit_ts_redo, relmap_redo,<br/>smgr_redo, heap_xlog_visible,<br/>xact_redo_commit/abort)
    end

    Startup->>Startup: PromoteIsTriggered()?<br/>Reach end of WAL?

    Startup->>SLRU: TrimCLOG()<br/>zeros the rest of the<br/>last accessed page
    Startup->>SLRU: TrimMultiXact()<br/>same for offsets+members

    Startup->>CF: UpdateControlFile<br/>(state = DB_IN_PRODUCTION)
    Startup->>Postmaster: ready;<br/>broadcast PM_RUN

    Postmaster->>Standby: open for connections
